    goingDeeper: "Coding-decoding questions almost always rely on one of a small number of underlying patterns: a fixed letter-shift (each letter moves forward/backward a fixed number of positions in the alphabet), a reversal, or a position-based rearrangement - spending a few minutes explicitly practicing 'find the shift' as its own drill (rather than only solving full questions) builds the specific sub-skill that makes the full questions fast, the same 'isolate the atomic skill' principle that applies to practicing scales before playing a full piece of music.",
