    commonMistakes: ["Assuming lexical analysis checks whether code is grammatically valid (like matching parentheses) - that's parsing's job, the NEXT phase; the lexer only groups characters into tokens, with no structural understanding yet", "Thinking whitespace/comments are passed along to later compiler phases - the lexer discards them entirely, since they carry no meaning for anything downstream"],
