    goingDeeper: "Even MFA has a genuine, well-known weak point worth knowing: SMS-based OTP codes are vulnerable to 'SIM swapping' (an attacker social-engineering a phone carrier into transferring your phone number to a device they control) - this is precisely why security-conscious systems increasingly prefer authenticator APPS (generating time-based codes locally on your device, never transmitted over the phone network at all) or hardware security keys over SMS specifically, as a genuinely stronger 'something you have' factor.",
