    assignment: "List three real-world systems you use regularly that are genuinely distributed systems, and for each one, identify at least one of this lesson's three core challenges (no shared clock, independent failures, unreliable messaging) that its designers must have addressed.",
    goingDeeper: "The theoretical foundations covered in this subject (Lamport clocks, Paxos/Raft, two-phase commit) were largely developed in the 1970s-1990s, well before most of today's largest distributed systems existed - genuinely worth appreciating that modern systems like Google Spanner, etcd (used by Kubernetes), and Apache Kafka are direct, practical engineering implementations of exactly these decades-old theoretical algorithms, not novel inventions unique to those specific products.",
