    goingDeeper: "The explainability concern connects directly and concretely back to this subject's own earlier lessons: an expert system's explicit IF-THEN rules are genuinely, inherently more explainable (you can trace exactly which rule fired and why) than many modern Machine Learning models (covered in this platform's own separate ML subject), whose internal decision process can be genuinely difficult to fully interpret even for the engineers who built them - this exact explainability trade-off is a real, active, ongoing consideration in choosing between classical AI and modern ML approaches for genuinely high-stakes real-world applications (like medical diagnosis or loan approval decisions).",
