    goingDeeper: "The F1 SCORE combines precision and recall into one single number (their harmonic mean), genuinely useful when you want ONE metric balancing both concerns rather than tracking two separate numbers - and the PRECISION-RECALL TRADE-OFF is itself worth knowing precisely: adjusting a classifier's decision threshold (like requiring 90% confidence instead of 50% before predicting 'positive') genuinely trades precision for recall or vice versa, letting you deliberately tune a real classifier's behavior toward whichever error type (false positives or false negatives) is genuinely more costly for your specific real-world application.",
