    assignment: "Explain, in your own words, why checking if (code1 AND code2) is non-zero correctly identifies that a line segment is entirely invisible, using the region-code bit meanings (top/bottom/left/right) to justify your reasoning.",
    goingDeeper: "The SUTHERLAND-HODGMAN algorithm extends this same clipping idea from line segments to entire POLYGONS, clipping a polygon against each of the four window boundary edges in sequence, one edge at a time, progressively trimming the polygon's vertex list down to just the portion actually inside the visible window - a genuinely necessary extension for real 3D graphics systems, which need to clip entire filled shapes/meshes, not just individual line segments.",
