    assignment: "For a small e-commerce business, describe one concrete security control serving each CIA Triad goal (confidentiality, integrity, availability), and explain why all three are genuinely necessary together.",
    goingDeeper: "Some security frameworks extend the CIA Triad with additional goals like NON-REPUDIATION (ensuring someone genuinely cannot later, falsely deny having performed a specific action - typically achieved via digital signatures/audit logs) and AUTHENTICATION (verifying someone genuinely is who they claim to be, before even considering what they're authorized to access) - worth knowing as a natural extension of the core CIA framework, since real security incidents frequently hinge specifically on being able to definitively prove (or disprove) who actually did what, and when.",
