    assignment: "For a healthcare company handling patient medical records, identify which compliance framework(s) it would need to satisfy, and describe two concrete security policies it should have in place for its employees.",
    goingDeeper: "The PRINCIPLE OF LEAST PRIVILEGE is a genuinely foundational security-policy concept worth knowing precisely, underlying many specific policies covered in this lesson: every employee/system/process should be granted ONLY the minimum access genuinely necessary to perform its specific, legitimate function, and nothing more - directly limiting the genuine real-world damage a single compromised account or insider threat could actually cause, since that compromised access is deliberately, structurally restricted to only what that specific role genuinely needed in the first place, rather than broad, unrestricted access to everything.",
